C3-responses-stream rigor-verified 2026-06-30 (no source change, no gap). Translator: _translate_chat_stream_to_responses (gateway main.py:8192), SSE framing helper _responses_sse (main.py:8188) = `event: <t>
data: {json}

`. Canonical typed lifecycle: response.created -> response.in_progress -> output_item.added -> content_part.added -> output_text.delta* -> output_text.done -> output_item.done -> response.completed -> [DONE]. TWO failure paths both -> terminal response.failed (status=failed, .response.error set, output_text='' so partial NEVER leaks, no phantom completed): (a) chat `error` dict frame (e.g. code output_blocked, clears accumulated), (b) terminal zeroshield.action=='error' trace frame (upstream mid-stream drop, main.py:8246, D5-RESP-STREAM-UPSTREAM-ERROR). finish_reason=='length' -> status 'incomplete'. Gate: cd gateway && ./.venv/bin/python -m pytest ai_mesh_gateway/tests/test_openai_sdk_compat.py -q -> 46 passed/2 xpassed (2 = documented non-strict D4/D5 cells). Coverage: harness cells test_responses_streaming_events_and_text + test_responses_mid_stream_failure_surfaces_typed_response_failed; upstream-error path in test_p2_phase6_holes.py::test_responses_stream_zeroshield_error_emits_failed_not_completed. Independent oracle probe: call translator directly, parse RAW bytes (assert exact event:/data: framing + body.type==event-name + canonical order), and drive stock SDK on a length stream -> status==incomplete (edge suite doesn't drive via SDK). Run a non-pytest probe with PYTHONPATH=$PWD:$PWD/../shared using gateway/.venv.
